{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1071964-antagonists","id":1071964,"title":"Antagonists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-02T03:11:47-07:00","id":1071964,"title":"Antagonists","content":"Who are your favorite antagonists in a VtR game and why?<br /> Whether they'e vampires, strix, hunters or something else doesn't matter. Not does it matter if they're from an official VtR book or if they're characters of your own creation. <br /> I'm interested in your experiences at the table with said antagonists. Who are they? How did you use them? And what made them work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3448-monkeymann","name":"MonkeyMann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T13:50:29-07:00","id":1072166,"title":"","content":"Depends on what I need them for. I do like using human mob and slashers as filler villains because they can be quickly disposed off and no one will lose daysleep over them.<br /> <br /> If I would have to chose I would say Belials Brood and VII because I can still give them some reasonable motivations(or make them deliciously evil). This is where Strix kinda fail for me because they are just random monster manual monsters that don't even drop nice loot. Same with Draugur/Larvae","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T14:01:09-07:00","id":1072168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orzhov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1071964-antagonists?p=1072166#post1072166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on what I need them for. I do like using human mob and slashers as filler villains because they can be quickly disposed off and no one will lose daysleep over them.<br /> <br /> If I would have to chose I would say Belials Brood and VII because I can still give them some reasonable motivations(or make them deliciously evil). This is where Strix kinda fail for me because they are just random monster manual monsters that don't even drop nice loot. Same with Draugur/Larvae</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree about the motivations of the Strix. I find them quite compelling, and they're my favorite vampire antagonists when used sparingly. That said, a little Strix goes a long way and they get dull when overused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T17:57:03-07:00","id":1072272,"title":"","content":"Normal mortals for cannon fodder, experienced hunters for shaking things up a little, other vampires for political intrigue, Strix for both petty evil and exploring the vampiric condition, Belial's Brood for exploring human sin, and other supernatural splats for throwing curve balls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T00:31:31-07:00","id":1072392,"title":"","content":"So far my best Vampire antagonists are a group of my own creation heavily ripped off of what I've read about the Masquerade, I even borrowed the name San Giovani. In this case they are a dynasty of Vampires obsessed with the veil of Death and with flesh crafting. In the past they masqueraded as a powerful Italian Trading House who helped bankroll Hitler's war machine in exchange for open access to the Concentration Camps, where they performed their death and flesh crafting experiments without reservation or restraint.<br /> \u200bAfter Hitler's fall they escaped notice, reinventing themselves as a modern corporate conglomerate (loosely modeled after the Umbrella Corporation from Resident Evil). Their obsessions remain the same but are now hidden behind medical research labs and third world dictators. Their ultimate goal (other than becoming Gods in the flesh) is to find a way to mass produce the perfect undead, flesh crafted armies, they are researching using highly virulent viruses to affect the changes.<br /> \u200bAs a conspiracy they are insanely wealthy, brilliant, immoral and not the least bit restrained by the limits of sanity. They have a global reach and point of view, meaning that when they work behind the scenes in Vampire society they don't care who sits on the throne, as long as they can ensure the security of their own possessions. They also have members recruited from all of the clans.<br /> \u200bJust for fluff they have a secret cadre of enforcers who still play at being the SS, complete with German Boar knives. One of my players made a game of collecting those knives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T19:57:54-07:00","id":1072892,"title":"","content":"The one i invented was something i feel lacked from Requiem, the sabbath. Not the whole sabbath with everything that entails but the narrative function the shovel heads served. An disposable enemy the PC can kill off by the truckload to take a break from all the politics and human drama. So the character who has vigor 4 or 5 and celerity can vent a little.<br /> <br /> So i modified the Brides of Dracula as a Carthian anarchist experiment gone wrong, who were a minor nuissance until they raided a Wyrm nest and got that ritual from the ordo dracul for mass embrace, and then they became a present danger ala sabbath. I even use Count Motherfucking dracula as construct created by the brides for figurehead, who instead of mind he has a narrative he follows (and is also why he reffers to himself in 3rd person) as the player who diablerize him found out.<br /> <br /> How i used them? For one i used them as the unifying factor for the other covenants to at least pretend to play nice. With the Carthians and Ordo focusing in hidding their asses from the mess they think they created (each dont know the other had a part on them) as quickly as possible. And the lancea gaining power playing crusaders while the Invictus is confused as to why everything seems fine and on-fire at the same time. <br /> <br /> For another is used them to empathize the dangers of &quot;leaving the city&quot;. And finally i used them as the chaos factor, the thing that unexpectedly shakes the plots &amp; plans of the elder vampires.<br /> <br /> Why they work so far? For one as i said before, they give a contrast to all the politics and drama. By taking a break from it to have some fun just killing a bunch of Briders with lots of ultraviolence or smart thinking makes them energized to coming back to deal with the plots of humanity or politics. They are never a central part but a healthy filler to gain some breathing room. For another they serves a mystery to solve, upon their second appearance in the game i made sure for the players to see that something was not quite as it seems with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T01:44:03-07:00","id":1072997,"title":"","content":"I adore the Strix because they so powerfully back up Requiem's core themes: they're the monster lurking just underneath the surface of every single one of the Kindred, a stark look into what the Beast looks like when not chained by Humanity. That would be harrowing enough on its own, but the paranoia aspect - they could be among you, and their runaway cruelty really doesn't look all that different from how the undead already act until it's too late - is both rich narrative material by itself and also helps to explain why Kindred society is so vicious and mistrusting. They remind the undead that no matter how scary they pretend to be, the real horrors are out there, and they're much, much older than the eldest among them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T06:29:47-07:00","id":1073076,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">double post</span><br /> </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T06:29:47-07:00","id":1073077,"title":"","content":"quadruple post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T14:00:26-07:00","id":1073348,"title":"","content":"Together with my friends we tend to play in a way each NPC is a potential antagonist or a friend. One ST created a character sheet for each vampire in a very big domain. More or less 25 characters, each has his or hers own character sheet with banes, aspirations and even a short description and a history. The most important retainers and foes have their own too.<br /> It gives a huge potential for a political chronicle, since the ST could improvise each time, but this way every single character in the domain has his own secrets, friends and enemies.<br /> Players may decide do they want to play in separate covenants as a potential enemies or play more friendly style for instance in one covenant and try to take over the city.<br /> <br /> As it comes to the antagonist Strix are a great tool for a ST, because almost every single vampire fears them. It makes Kindred feel that they are not on the very end of the food chain. I have a feeling that in CoD Strix took VIIs place as the most dangerous enemy. The Strix can be very chaotic in its plans, it might pretend to be a vampire for fun or just create chaos all the time. Who knows maybe the prince is possesed by the powerful Strix since 1900s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T12:55:48-07:00","id":1078487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edgar McAlister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1071964-antagonists?p=1073348#post1073348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Together with my friends we tend to play in a way each NPC is a potential antagonist or a friend. One ST created a character sheet for each vampire in a very big domain. More or less 25 characters, each has his or hers own character sheet with banes, aspirations and even a short description and a history. The most important retainers and foes have their own too.<br /> It gives a huge potential for a political chronicle, since the ST could improvise each time, but this way every single character in the domain has his own secrets, friends and enemies.<br /> Players may decide do they want to play in separate covenants as a potential enemies or play more friendly style for instance in one covenant and try to take over the city.</div> </div> </div> </div><i><b>Only 25 Vampires</b></i>? That is a <i><b>SMALL </b></i>domain. Wow...<br /> I think that on last count there were 130 vampires in the campaign I have working. And that is just for the Kindred of the Domain. Does not include the Mages (about 40 or so), Werewolves (close to 50), or Changelings (52 or so) that are tromping around there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T15:12:44-07:00","id":1078568,"title":"","content":"The average number of vampires in any given domain varies wildly from one table to another, depending both on how many vampires is considered realistic per capita, and how populous a big domain is considered to be by the players.<br /> If we were to use &quot;1% of 1%&quot; as a rule of thumb only three cities in the entirety of Sweden would be able to house more than 15 vampires, in contrast to London which would house over a thousand vampires using the very same rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-14-2017, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T17:17:11-07:00","id":1078650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1071964-antagonists?p=1078487#post1078487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i><b>Only 25 Vampires</b></i>? That is a <i><b>SMALL </b></i>domain. Wow...<br /> I think that on last count there were 130 vampires in the campaign I have working. And that is just for the Kindred of the Domain. Does not include the Mages (about 40 or so), Werewolves (close to 50), or Changelings (52 or so) that are tromping around there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>1. We play in the XIX century, so cities are much smaller.<br /> 2. The chronicle is rather not so supernatural in terms of number of other supernatural beings (at least the vampires think that way).<br /> 3. The ruling vampires don't like newcomers too much, since it can change the balance of power.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> assumed as a rule of thumb that 1% of population can be supernatural. We use a different rule. I'm not sure if it was in Vampire Requiem 1st edition or Masquerade, but there was a rule 12 vampires per 100 000 city population.<br /> <br /> To sum up, the domain is <b>relatively </b>big. Ofc there are bigger domains, but the rule &quot;12 vampires per 100 000&quot; makes sense, due to the 1st Tradition. The Prince or ruling vampires shouldn't overpopulate their domain with unnatural beings, but it's only my opinion you guys can rule differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","user":"Edgar McAlister","date":". 04-14-2017, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T18:32:13-07:00","id":1078690,"title":"","content":"1% of 1% was just an example. My first point was that different tables use different population rates since there's, to my knowledge, no published population rates in CofD in either edition. 1% of 1% is just a rate I've seen pop up a few times in this forum, but people can (and has) changed it an order of magnitude in either direction to fit their own games, and that's quite fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T20:04:33-07:00","id":1078727,"title":"","content":"There was in first edition but it's been left by the wayside. People keep trying to insist upon one.<br /> <br /> 25 can seem small but it can be just right. Do what's good for the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T00:47:03-07:00","id":1078798,"title":"","content":"Somewhere I read 1 on 100000 and 1 on 60000 in the most populated city. To me vampire shouldn't be too much. I don't like Blade superpopoluation of vampire <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. <br /> They are monster and demigod of darkness. If you have hundreds of such monsters they become less &quot;special&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T02:34:49-07:00","id":1078811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1071964-antagonists?p=1078798#post1078798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somewhere I read 1 on 100000 and 1 on 60000 in the most populated city. To me vampire shouldn't be too much. I don't like Blade superpopoluation of vampire <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> They are monster and demigod of darkness. If you have hundreds of such monsters they become less &quot;special&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like overpopulated domains myself. As it come to the population rates, in modern times the biggest cities can have more than 100 vampires. In CoD VtR we can read that Tokyo boast over 300 Kindred (XX or XXI century)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T07:42:25-07:00","id":1083011,"title":"","content":"I don't like the Strix and in my games, they don't exist. But I do find plenty of mileage out of other antagonists such as Belial's Brood. VII can be okay too if you want to shake things up and alter the power structure of a city (especially since I just go with the vague unknowable VII from the 1e corebook, never really cared for the Betrayed or the Akhud), and even the playable covenants can make for good antagonists depending which side you're on. In a Circle of the Crone-focused game, the Lancea Sanctum make excellent villains, as does the Invictus.<br /> <br /> I am currently planning a chronicle in which the Ascending Ones from Hunter: The Vigil are the main antagonists with Belial's Brood as a secondary minor antagonist.<br /> <br /> I always saw the Strix as overpowered and kind of pointless. There's plenty of dangers for vampires out there. Fire, sunlight, hunters, the cops, other vampires, they don't need some invincible owls with no real motive to be present. But if you like the Strix, feel free to use them. It's your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T16:52:33-07:00","id":1083226,"title":"","content":"Strix are kinda overpowered, but their role is to be the nastiest of all antagonists. They might exist, but be only a legend and players won't encounter them. Personally I like that every player fears them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T05:37:03-07:00","id":1083928,"title":"","content":"I like weird things that have implications about vampires by their very existence and nature. Certainly Strix fit this role, but they're too ingrained in kindred culture for those that know where to look. In this particular situation, I've yet to see psychic vampires used in this capacity, or else use them in a chronicle I've ST'd myself. However, it is a tempting idea given that a number of their powers are rather similar to disciplines. Jiang Shi also have an interesting capability to be used for this, perhaps a conspiracy of them with greater knowledge of the kindred condition. Their origins are unusual enough that it does raise questions about lots of things. How did vampires come to be? Why are there so many differences? Are they similar creatures? Species in the scientific classification sense, where &quot;Kindred&quot; is essentially the genus? Lots of questions when you toy with the definition of what a vampire is by way of clans that are JUST different enough. Even drawing those... Forget what they were called, Leech hosts from Werewolf into the picture could be neat if only because they heavily resemble the Pijavica. Or maybe those ARE Pijavica and the werewolves are misunderstanding what's going on. Possibilities abound!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}